[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Generated bounded integer requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-011-GEN-DECLARE
TITLE: Validate generated domain declarations
STATEMENT: >>>
The generator shall emit a bounded domain only for a supported top-level partial struct,
a built-in integer storage type, an ordered decimal interval representable in that storage,
and valid annotation options. Invalid declarations and generated member name collisions
shall produce source diagnostics. Native bounds shall fit every architecture permitted
by the compilation platform and native storage identity shall survive application aliases.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/SharpSafeNumerics.Generator/BoundedIntegerGenerator.cs, CreateModel,
GetStorage, Literal and HintName. Verification: GeneratorCompilationTests diagnostics,
platform-specific extrema, XML documentation and namespace isolation.
Evidence: docs/GENERATOR_RC1.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-011-GEN-VALUE
TITLE: Domain validity and value semantics
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated domains shall distinguish an invalid default from admitted values unless ZeroValid
is declared with an interval containing zero. Instances shall expose safe extraction,
typed equality, hashing and total ordering, with invalid defaults ordered before valid
values. Generated declarations and public members shall include XML documentation and
the resulting type shall have a debugger display.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: NumericAnnotations.cs and BoundedIntegerGenerator.Rendering.cs, Render.
Verification: GeneratedDomainTests invalid and zero-valid defaults, equality and comparisons,
GeneratedContractTests cross-fixture checks and GeneratorCompilationTests generated documentation
and debugger display metadata.
The tests also verify that admission preserves unrelated user static fields.
Evidence: docs/GENERATOR_RC1.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-011-GEN-ARITH
TITLE: Generated arithmetic policies and rejecting Try paths
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated TryAdd and TrySubtract shall report invalid operands, primitive overflow
or underflow and out-of-domain results with a status and default output.
Generated Add and Subtract shall consume the annotated policy. Reject shall preserve
failure statuses, Saturate shall clamp to the inclusive domain, Wrap shall apply
primitive modulo arithmetic and then require domain membership, and Throw shall raise
OverflowException when the primitive result overflows or falls outside the domain.
An invalid instance shall yield Uninitialized for every policy.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: BoundedIntegerGenerator.Rendering.cs, Render and RenderArithmeticAdmission.
Verification: GeneratedDomainTests arithmetic tests for all policies and invalid instances,
and GeneratedContractTests independent arithmetic oracle for primitive and domain boundaries.
Evidence: docs/GENERATOR_RC1.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-011-GEN-CONVERT
TITLE: Exact generated conversions
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated conversion methods shall preserve exactly representable built-in integer values,
enforce domain admission on entry, and clear outputs on rejection. A cast between the
domain and its storage shall be explicit and enforce admission or instance validity.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: BoundedIntegerGenerator.Rendering.cs, Render, delegating to SafeInteger.TryConvert.
Verification: GeneratedDomainTests exact conversion, sign, storage and domain range, and cast tests.
Evidence: docs/GENERATOR_RC1.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-011-GEN-TEXT
TITLE: Invariant span text and unit metadata
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated span text methods shall use the configured invariant decimal or hexadecimal
convention, reject malformed and out-of-domain input, and report no characters written
on insufficient capacity or invalid value. Optional unit metadata shall be available
without runtime reflection and shall leave values, parsing and formatting unchanged.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: NumericAnnotations.cs and BoundedIntegerGenerator.Rendering.cs, Render.
Verification: GeneratedDomainTests culture, unit metadata, hexadecimal exhaustive test,
malformed-input cases, seeded suffix fuzzing and invariant round trips.
Evidence: docs/GENERATOR_RC1.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SN-011-GEN-BINARY
TITLE: Fixed-width binary codecs
STATEMENT: >>>
Generated span codecs shall read an exact-width little- or big-endian integer and require
domain membership before admission. A write shall preserve the configured signedness and
width and touch only the prefix it reports written. Invalid values or insufficient write
capacity shall fail without changing the destination. A binary width that cannot represent
the complete interval shall be diagnosed at compilation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: BoundedIntegerGenerator.cs, CreateModel and Fits, and
BoundedIntegerGenerator.Rendering.cs, RenderBinaryCodec.
Verification: GeneratorCompilationTests invalid widths and GeneratedDomainTests independent
BigInteger byte oracles, signed and unsigned extrema, and fixed-width failure cases in
GeneratedContractTests.
Evidence: docs/GENERATOR_RC1.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: SN-011
